<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    Cast campaign, the (long)v residue `castindex`: a pointer plus a VARIABLE
    index, and the difference of two byte pointers, are printed as integer
    round trips.  coreutils sort -O0 `mergefps` (sub_a5c0) prints

        *(long *)((long)v7 + v19 * 8) = v10 + -0x20;

    and ls -O0 `print_long_format` (sub_c6c8) prints

        sub_5453(v14,(long)v24 - (long)v14);

    where the same arithmetic is element v19 of a `long *` and the byte
    difference of two `char *`.  Root cause (P9, ActionSetCasts): castarith
    keeps only a pointer plus a CONSTANT in pointer terms; a variable addend
    reaches the cast pass as the same INT_ADD, priced as integer arithmetic
    (`(long)` in, a cast back out), and an INT_SUB's operands are converted to
    `long` by the default input-cast rule.

    Stage / sub-stage: P9 "casts".  The P0 assertion `option castindex on|off`
    decides whether such a sum, used as a `T *` with a scale of sizeof(T),
    becomes PTRADD(base, i, #sizeof T), and whether a difference of two
    pointers to the same byte type keeps its operands uncast.

    The fixture (SysV x86-64):

        ldidx:  movsxd rsi,esi; mov eax,[rdi+rsi*4]     an int index, 4-byte
                add eax,[rdi+8]                          elements (the constant
                                                         read makes rdi void *)
        ld64:   mov rax,[rdi+rsi*8]; add rax,[rdi+0x10]  a long index
        ldbyte: movzx eax,byte [rdi+rsi]; add eax,[rdi+4] a byte index
        rec16:  movsxd; shl rsi,4; mov rax,[rdi+rsi+8]   a 16-byte record read at
                                                         8 bytes: the scale is not
                                                         the element, so the
                                                         integer form stays
        diff:   call strchr; sub rax,rbx                 strchr(s,c) - s

    Pass 1 (`option castindex off`) reproduces the bug; pass 2 turns it on.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000">

</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="ldidx"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100020" name="ld64"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100040" name="ldbyte"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100060" name="rec16"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100080" name="diff"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000c0" name="strchr"/>
</binaryimage>
