<stringmatch name="castindex #1: with the option off an int-indexed read through a void pointer is an integer round trip -- the bug" min="1" max="1">return \*\(int4 \*\)\(\(int8\)a0 \+ \(int8\)a1 \* 4\) \+ \(\(int4 \*\)a0\)\[2\];</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="castindex #2: and a byte-pointer difference converts both pointers to integers" min="1" max="1">return \(int8\)strchr\(a0,a1\) - \(int8\)a0;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="castindex #3: on, the int index is a subscript of the 4-byte element, and its extension is C's own" min="1" max="1">return \(\(int4 \*\)a0\)\[a1\] \+ \(\(int4 \*\)a0\)\[2\];</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="castindex #4: a long index is a subscript of the 8-byte element" min="1" max="1">return \(\(int8 \*\)a0\)\[a1\] \+ \(\(int8 \*\)a0\)\[2\];</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="castindex #5: a byte read takes the variable itself as the index" min="1" max="1">return \(uint4\)\(\(uint1 \*\)a0\)\[a1\] \+ \(\(int4 \*\)a0\)\[1\];</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="castindex #6: a 16-byte stride read at 8 bytes keeps the integer form in both passes" min="2" max="2">return \*\(int8 \*\)\(\(int8\)a0 \+ \(int8\)a1 \* 0x10 \+ 8\) \+ \(\(int8 \*\)a0\)\[2\];</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="castindex #7: on, the difference of two char pointers is C's own pointer subtraction" min="1" max="1">return strchr\(a0,a1\) - a0;</stringmatch>
